Maybe some of you have heard about that great french comic called "donjon"
(translated into english as "dungeon") (*). Well, this tell the story
about a big dungeon filled with treasure where many adventurer come,
seeking glory or fortune and end up being killed by the monsters (some of
them escape with some treasure, this goes on the "advertisment" budget of
the dungeon...) All of this being told from the dungeon keeper (and
monsters) point of view.

Anyway, in this dungeon, the chief of the guards and maybe one of the most
powerful inhabitant is a red draconian fighter with awesome powers called
"Marvin". But he usually never use an escape route.



(*) By L. Trondheim, J. Sfarr and much much more. Around 30 hardcovers
have been published in french (by Delcourt) and I've seen it under
translation in the US, the first two books being sold as one "duck's
heart") and the third and fourth being under publication in a specialized
magazine (well, the way US comics often are published, AFAIK). I don't
know how the US translation plan to handle the messy timeline and the puns
in the titles...
See http://www.pastis.org/donjonland/ for more detail (in french).

